    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "models/gemini-3-flash-preview",
          "cachedResultName": "Gemini 3 Flash Preview",
          "cachedResultUrl": ""
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=ROLE: You are a project management office analyst assisting a project manager.\n\nTASK: Read the meeting transcript below and extract (1) action items and (2) risks, issues, decisions and scope changes.\n\nCONTEXT: Project is the BrightMart CRM rollout. The meeting name and date are given in the transcript header. Convert the header date to YYYY-MM-DD, and use it to interpret relative dates such as \"Monday\" or \"Friday\".\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Use ONLY information stated in the transcript. Never invent owners, dates, risks or facts.\n- Only log a risk or issue if a speaker raised it or described a clear delay, blocker or dependency. Do not log a plain status update as a risk or issue. Do not create risks from your own inference.\n- Log one item per underlying problem. Never log the same problem twice (for example as both an Issue and a Risk). A Scope Change is logged once, as a Scope Change only.\n- Use type \"Decision\" only when a speaker states that something was decided, approved or agreed. An open question, or a fact someone is unsure about, is an Issue, not a Decision.\n- type must be one of: Risk, Issue, Decision, Scope Change.\n- Put a mitigation inside the item's \"mitigation\" field. Create a separate action only when a named person commits to doing something or is asked to do it.\n\nDATES AND OWNERS (actions):\n- If a weekday or relative day is stated (\"Wednesday\", \"by Monday\"), convert it to YYYY-MM-DD and flag DATE_INFERRED.\n- If an explicit calendar date is stated (\"by 24 March\"), convert it to YYYY-MM-DD and flag NONE.\n- If the timing is vague (\"soon\", \"this week\", \"end of next week\", \"roughly\") or depends on another event, set due_date to null, keep the original words in due_date_raw_text, and flag DATE_UNCLEAR.\n- For a recurring commitment (\"every Friday\"), set due_date to null, put the recurrence in due_date_raw_text, and flag NONE.\n- If no person is named for an action, set owner to null and flag OWNER_MISSING. If a person is named, never use OWNER_MISSING.\n- CONFLICTING_INFO = two speakers contradict each other, or one speaker is explicitly unsure between options (\"six or maybe eight\"). Dependence on another event is not a conflict.\n- Several flags may be combined, separated by commas. Use NONE if nothing is wrong.\n\nFLAGS FOR ITEMS: use ONLY CONFLICTING_INFO or NONE. Never use OWNER_MISSING, DATE_INFERRED or DATE_UNCLEAR on an item.\n\nSEVERITY: allowed values are High, Medium, Low, Unrated, or null. Use \"Unrated\" unless a speaker explicitly gave a rating or described the impact as high, medium, low, critical, major or minor. Never assign severity yourself. Use null for Decisions.\n\nQUOTES: source_quote must be a short verbatim quote (under 20 words) from the speaker who describes the item, and it must directly support the description. Escape any double quotation marks inside text values.\n\nNULLS: Use null (not an empty string) for any unknown owner, date, date text, severity or mitigation.\n\n- Extract EVERY action and EVERY risk, issue, decision and scope change mentioned. Never leave an item out because its owner is unclear. For each item, fill owner with the person who raised it or is named to resolve it, using the full name from the attendee list. If no person fits, use null, but still include the item.\n\nOUTPUT: Return ONLY one valid JSON object. No markdown, no code fences, no explanation, no trailing commas. Use exactly this shape:\n{\n \"meeting_name\": \"\",\n \"meeting_date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n \"actions\": [\n  {\"description\": \"\", \"owner\": null, \"due_date\": null, \"due_date_raw_text\": null, \"flag\": \"NONE\", \"source_quote\": \"\"}\n ],\n \"items\": [\n  {\"type\": \"\", \"description\": \"\", \"severity\": \"Unrated\", \"mitigation\": null, \"owner\": null, \"flag\": \"NONE\", \"source_quote\": \"\"}\n ]\n}\n\nTRANSCRIPT:\n{{ $json.transcript }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "78cd7fc5-8eb9-432a-af2f-11d90bd5afb3",
      "name": "Message a model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        32,
        32
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const v = x => (x === null || x === undefined) ? '' : x;\nconst loggedAt = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace('T', ' ');\nconst num = n => String(n + 1).padStart(2, '0');\n\nfunction scopeNote(type, desc) {\n  const d = v(desc);\n  if (type === 'Scope Change' && !/not\\s+(yet\\s+)?approved/i.test(d)) {\n    return d + ' [Not approved - decision pending]';\n  }\n  return d;\n}\n\nfunction fixFlag(flag, owner, isAction) {\n  let f = String(flag || 'NONE').split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(s => s && s !== 'NONE' && s !== 'OWNER_MISSING');\n  if (isAction && !owner) f.push('OWNER_MISSING');\n  return f.length ? f.join(', ') : 'NONE';\n}\n\nconst rows = [];\n\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const raw = item.json;\n  const parts = raw.content?.parts ?? [];\n  let text = parts.map(p => p.text ?? '').join('') || raw.text || raw.output || '';\n  text = text.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\n  text = text.slice(text.indexOf('{'), text.lastIndexOf('}') + 1);\n  const data = JSON.parse(text);\n\n  (data.actions || []).forEach((a, i) => rows.push({ json: {\n    kind: 'action',\n    id: `A-${data.meeting_date}-${num(i)}`,\n    source_meeting: v(data.meeting_name),\n    meeting_date: v(data.meeting_date),\n    description: v(a.description),\n    owner: v(a.owner),\n    due_date: v(a.due_date),\n    due_date_raw_text: v(a.due_date_raw_text),\n    flag: fixFlag(a.flag, a.owner, true),\n    source_quote: v(a.source_quote),\n    status: 'Open',\n    logged_at: loggedAt\n  }}));\n\n  (data.items || []).forEach((it, i) => rows.push({ json: {\n    kind: 'item',\n    id: `R-${data.meeting_date}-${num(i)}`,\n    source_meeting: v(data.meeting_name),\n    type: v(it.type),\n    description: scopeNote(it.type, it.description),\n    severity: v(it.severity),\n    mitigation: v(it.mitigation),\n    owner: v(it.owner),\n    flag: fixFlag(it.flag, it.owner, false),\n    source_quote: v(it.source_quote),\n    logged_at: loggedAt\n  }}));\n}\n\nreturn rows;"
      },
